From bdaa00ded45a8ca7802be2055c0b4e18d4337ebf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:42:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 102/206] feat(shorebird): real self_hash in --shorebird, and
 our SHA-1 was broken
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The three hashes were a placeholder -- all three carried sha1 of the raw
instruction bytes, with "simplified" in the comment. self_hash is now the
reconstructed algorithm: SHA-1 over a stream of {kind, value} entries, ported
from the model in probe_subgraph_hash.py.

Porting it uncovered a worse bug. The port produced entry streams byte-identical
to the Python model and still disagreed on every digest, which left only one
candidate: FhpSHA1 was not SHA-1.

  #define FF(i,f,k) t=...; e=d; d=c; c=FhpRot(b,30); b=a; a=t

Six statements, no do/while(0), and every use is an unbraced `for` body. Only
the t= was in the loop; the whole variable rotation ran once, after it. A
function that looks like SHA-1, compiles clean, runs without complaint, and
produces digests nothing else in the world agrees with. Fixed, with the reason
in a comment so it does not get "tidied" back.

Results, measured:

  C++ port vs the validated Python model      1589 / 1589
  vs THEIR self_hash, joined by name+size      777 / 950

The second number is the real one and it is a cross-implementation check, not a
self-comparison: for functions present in both snapshots at the same size, 82%
of our hashes equal Shorebird's. That tracks the model's known 1185/1380, and
the shortfall is the same unsolved piece -- ordinals that depend on the callee
walk.

⚠️ subgraph_hash and op_subgraph_hash still carry self_hash and are wrong. The
keys stay so the schema matches theirs, and the comment says plainly that the
values do not. They need the walk, which task 30 established is a much larger
job.

Negative control: rotating by 29 instead of 30 turns the check red on the first
entry's hash. Restored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

